\title{covstructs7: An S7 Framework for Constrained Matrix Parameters}
\description{
Parametrisations of covariance-adjacent constrained matrix spaces as objects. A structure maps an unconstrained vector to a symmetric matrix -- positive definite, a correlation matrix, or a possibly rank-deficient precision -- and answers with exact first and second derivatives, the log-determinant or its pseudo-determinant counterpart, and the solves a likelihood needs. Numerical fallbacks make a user-defined structure work from its map alone, and a diagnostic verifies every component against an independent route.
